=========================================================
PART E: Find and fix
=========================================================

1. grade(85) returns 'C'. The first check (mark >= 50) is already true
   for 85, so it returns before reaching the 70 and 80 checks.

2. isPalindrome('level') gives a RangeError. At i = 0 it reads
   word[word.length - 0] = word[5], but the last index is 4.

3. Lines I changed:
   grade: I swapped the first and last branches so the highest check
   comes first (4 lines: the >= 50 and >= 80 conditions and their returns).
     if (mark >= 80) { return 'A'; }
     else if (mark >= 70) { return 'B'; }
     else if (mark >= 50) { return 'C'; }
   isPalindrome (1 line):
     if (word[i].toLowerCase() != word[word.length - 1 - i].toLowerCase()) return false;

4. I chose true for 'Level'. A palindrome is about the letters, not
   about capital or small letters. My code matches because it changes
   both letters to lowercase before comparing.

