=========================================================
PART G: Debugging log
=========================================================

Error 1: RangeError in isPalindrome
Exact error: RangeError (index): Index out of range: index should be less than 10: 10
Line: if (word[i] != word[word.length - i]) return false;
Cause: When i = 0, it reads word[word.length - 0] which is word[5] for
"level", but the last valid index is 4. Off-by-one error.
Fix: Changed word[word.length - i] to word[word.length - 1 - i].

Error 2: RangeError in initials with extra spaces
Exact error: RangeError (index): Index out of range: index should be less than 0: 0
Line: result += '${parts[i][0].toUpperCase()}.';
Cause: Splitting ' ana uwase ' on a single space produced empty
strings like '', and reading [0] of an empty string crashes.
Fix: Changed split(' ') to split(RegExp(r'\s+')) and added trim()
before splitting, plus a check if (parts[i].isNotEmpty).

Error 3: grade(85) returning the wrong value
Exact wrong output: grade(85) returned 'C' instead of 'A'
Line: if (mark >= 50) { return 'C'; } (this was the first condition)
Cause: The conditions were in the wrong order. Since 85 >= 50 is true,
it returned 'C' without checking 70 or 80.
Fix: Reordered the conditions from highest to lowest: >= 80 first,
then >= 70, then >= 50.

Which question took the longest:
Part F (MoMo simulator) took the longest because formatRwf had to group
digits in threes without any library, so I had to think carefully about
the index math. Getting the comma placement right for numbers like
1,000,000 took several tries. isValidPin was also tricky because I had
to handle many rejection conditions in the right order.